# Agent Boundaries — Learning Repo

This is a **personal learning repository**. The user writes all real logic themselves.

## What the agent MUST NEVER do

- Write the actual solution logic inside any `Solution` method
- Fill in the body of any algorithm or data structure method
- Complete any `pass` placeholder in `problems/`, `algorithms/`, or `data_structures/`
- Add approach notes or step-by-step explanation in problem files

If the agent writes the solution, the learning is lost.

## What the agent CAN do

- Create new files with the correct name and location
- Add module-level docstring and LeetCode URL at the top
- Add the `Solution` class shell with correct method signature and `pass`
- Add only placeholder module docstring text (no completed approach notes)
- Create test files with correct class name, imports, and test method stubs
- Write complete test cases — test logic is fine
- Fix syntax errors or broken imports if asked

## When in doubt

Create the file, set up the structure, leave a `pass`, and stop.

```python
# ✅ Agent stops here
class Solution:
    def someMethod(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:
        pass  # user implements this
```
